# Qguard Helix Lightweight Agent & Collector Installer

## Enterprise-Grade Agent Deployment, Enrollment, Scanning, Telemetry & Migration Control Plane

Build and implement a **premium, enterprise-grade Lightweight Agent / Collector / Patcher / Operator installation system** for Qguard Helix.

The primary installation and management page must be:

`http://localhost:3000/downloads`

The system must integrate seamlessly with:

`http://localhost:3000/dashboard/scanner?tab=agents`

and the existing:

`http://localhost:3000/dashboard/live-migration`

The objective is to allow customers to securely generate, download, install, enroll, verify, operate, update, and manage lightweight Qguard Helix agents across their endpoints, servers, cloud workloads, containers, Kubernetes environments, and other authorized assets.

---

# 1. Core Objective

When an authenticated tenant creates an Agent / Collector / Patcher / Operator from:

`/dashboard/scanner?tab=agents`

the user must be able to:

1. Generate an agent.
2. Assign the agent to a tenant.
3. Assign it to an asset, asset group, environment, or scope.
4. Select the appropriate agent capability.
5. Generate a secure enrollment token.
6. Download the appropriate installer.
7. Install the lightweight agent on the target device.
8. Automatically enroll the agent.
9. Establish a secure authenticated connection with Qguard Helix.
10. Verify connectivity.
11. Run an initial discovery/crypto scan.
12. Stream telemetry to the backend.
13. Display accurate results in the Qguard Helix dashboard.
14. Detect cryptographic and quantum-vulnerability exposure.
15. Support approved remediation and migration operations.
16. Receive agent upgrades securely.
17. Report health, version, capabilities, and execution status.
18. Provide complete audit evidence for every operation.

This must behave as a **real operational system**, not a mock UI or static download page.

